Notes:
Data streams - Every program ran on the command line automatically has three data streams:
  STDIN (0) - Standard input (data fed into the program).
  STDOUT (1) - Standard output (data printed by the program).
  STDERR (2) - Standard error (for error messages).
Redirection - Uses greater than (>), signs to redirect the output to a file or directory or whatever. Can be used both ways.
Piping - Uses vertical line/pipe line (|), sign to feed the output from the program on the left as input to the program on the right.

